ywhere on the page (confirmed via browser_evaluate querying all `input` and `button` elements: only one text input and two buttons — 'New Resume' and the sort dropdown — exist). Users cannot filter saved resumes by exact creation date or date range.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No validation for invalid date ranges\", \"actual\": \"Set Experience Start Date = 2019-03 and End Date = 2018-01 (end precedes start). No error message or rejection occurred; the field accepted the value and the Live Preview rendered \\\"Mar 2019 - Jan 2018\\\" without any warning or blocking feedback.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Start/End Date inputs are native type=month controls (consistent MM/YYYY entry, rendered as \\\"Mar 2019 - Jun 2022\\\" in preview). Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared and disabled the End Date field, and preview showed \\\"Mar 2019 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Data not persisted across page reload\", \"actual\": \"Prior to reload, dashboard had 5 resumes: original 3 (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer) plus 'Marketing Resume - Acme' (newly created) and 'Sales Manager Resume' (a renamed duplicate). After navigating to http://localhost:6005/ via a fresh page load (browser_navigate), the dashboard reverted to showing only the original 3 resumes ('Product Designer Resume', 'Marketing Manager Resume', 'Software Engineer Resume') — the created and duplicated resumes were gone. Confirmed via browser_evaluate that localStorage and sessionStorage are both empty (no keys), indicating state is held only in-memory (e.g., React state) with no persistence layer, so created/edited/duplicated/renamed resumes do not survive a reload.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No validation feedback on empty rename\", \"actual\": \"Clearing the resume title and entering only whitespace, then pressing Enter, correctly reverted the title back to \\\"Marketing Resume - Acme\\\" (empty/whitespace title was not persisted). However, no error message, toast, or any validation feedback was shown to the user; the Notifications region remained empty throughout.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Every field edit (contact info, summary, experience, education, skills) was reflected in the Live Preview panel immediately after typing/selecting, with no save or refresh action required.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After reordering sections and hiding Education, switching editor tabs and navigating to the dashboard and back into the resume preserved the new order (Work Experience, Career Summary, Skills) and kept Education hidden.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard card showed \\\"Updated Aug 25, 2026\\\" (today) after edits, and reopening the resume from the dashboard restored all previously entered content without loss.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added 4 experience entries plus summary/education/skills content, exceeding the preview panel's initial ~798px height (content grew to ~1953px). Every visible populated section (Work Experience with all entries, Career Summary, Education, Skills) rendered with full content in the DOM/preview (verified via accessibility tree), and the page became scrollable (documentScrollHeight 2018 > viewport 720) so no content is clipped or permanently hidden — all sections remain reachable by scrolling.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Reopened \\\"Marketing Resume - Acme\\\" from dashboard after navigating away; Contact (Jane Smith, email, phone, location, LinkedIn, website), Summary, Experience (Acme Corp), Education (University of Texas) and Skills (Digital Marketing) all remained intact in both editor and preview.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After duplicating and renaming to 'Sales Manager Resume', edited the copy's Full Name to 'Jane Smith (Sales)'. The original 'Marketing Resume - Acme' retained its original Full Name 'Jane Smith' and all other content (Work Experience, Career Summary, Education, Skills) unchanged, confirming edits to the copy do not affect the original.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After renaming via the editor title field to \\\"Marketing Resume - Acme\\\", the editor showed the new title and the dashboard card also displays heading \\\"Marketing Resume - Acme\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized section heading not rendered in Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Renamed the Summary section heading to \\\"Career Summary\\\" in the Sections tab. Modern and Classic styles correctly render the \\\"Career Summary\\\" heading text above the summary paragraph. However, in the Minimal style the summary section renders only the paragraph text with no heading element at all (verified via DOM: <section><p>...</p></section>, no <h2>), so the customized heading is not shown even though the section is visible.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
      }
